{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/158702-advises-on-running-shadow-realm","id":158702,"title":"Advises on running Shadow Realm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-03T22:04:19-07:00","id":158702,"title":"Advises on running Shadow Realm","content":"So my Wolf-Blooded players will hunt for Totem in our next session. That means they are going in to Shadow. I got cool idea of keyed Verge on the frozen waterfall, I readied all about ecology of Realm and interaction with spirits, and I get whole &quot;<i>Princes Mononoke</i> meets <i>Sailent Hill&quot;</i> vibe of <i>Hisil</i>. But still I can't run smoothly the Shadow in my mind, even if I am normally <b>Mage</b> ST and can come up with very interesting solutions is my mark.<br /> <br /> I think the problem I have is, compared to the Hedge from <b>Changling</b>, Shadow Realm can't be &quot;edited&quot; - that mean's the setting is putting it &quot;it's mostly like Material World, only filled with monstrous spirits in place of humans&quot;. I just can't take out portions of game world I don't have cool ideas to run for, like I would in <b>Changling</b>, and on the other hand I don't have rough game map to make something on fly, like I was doing with <b>Silent Hill</b> game. <br /> <br /> Best indicates a problem my current situation - I have cool &quot;portal&quot; scene with frozen waterfall. I got disturbing and mysterious scene of first confrontation with would-be Totem. But I don't have ideas on 2-3 scenes of interaction and travel in between, so players would get they first taste of Shadow Realm, like in books. Any advises how to improve this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T22:28:46-07:00","id":158731,"title":"","content":"Describe the material place whose Shadow you hope to have them visit for the thread in terms of history, terrain, and resident flora and fauna. The point of the Shadow's locales being built on material ones is to take those qualities and turn up the symbolism instead of just throwing random ideas on the other side of a plot-gate. That's how the Shadow is <i>relevant.</i><br /> <br /> What things are important in the area? How is the Verge keyed? Is the place far from human population? If not, what is the human population like? If so, what kind of animals inhabit it? Are there any notable scenarios with the local spirit courts that impact the area?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T00:17:44-07:00","id":158798,"title":"","content":"As I was reading in corebook about Essence &quot;bribing&quot; of spirits from other choirs, I got those two encounters ideas:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Animal Spirit, probably Lynx or Arctic Fox, can be hostile to PCs.</li> <li>Half dormant Tree/Truck <i>magath, </i>created after jeep hit old spruce in accident. Car was abandoned and Spruce Spirit devoured it.</li> </ol>One more would be great for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/158702-advises-on-running-shadow-realm?p=158731#post158731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Describe the material place whose Shadow you hope to have them visit for the thread in terms of history, terrain, and resident flora and fauna.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's loosely <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sarek_National_Park\" target=\"_blank\">Sarek National Park</a> in Sweden. Local population are modern Swedes, but from Shadows perspective, important are more <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sami_people\" target=\"_blank\">Sami people</a>. Totem is Sami old star bear god. I got idea of Lynx and Arctic Fox spirits from Sarek Park description.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/158702-advises-on-running-shadow-realm?p=158731#post158731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What things are important in the area?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's created up to date, as needed setting. There aren't important things in area, as they aren't invented for the time being. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/158702-advises-on-running-shadow-realm?p=158731#post158731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is the Verge keyed?</div> </div> </div> </div>First rays of sunrise affects water under the waterfall, let it become gateway past Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/158702-advises-on-running-shadow-realm?p=158731#post158731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the place far from human population?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the middle of mountain range, next human settlement is few kilometers away, about hundred meter lower.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/158702-advises-on-running-shadow-realm?p=158731#post158731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If so, what kind of animals inhabit it?</div> </div> </div> </div>From Wikipedia:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The flora of this zone is constituted by <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primary_forest\" target=\"_blank\">primary forests</a> of conifers, principally the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scots_pine\" target=\"_blank\">Scots pine</a> (<i>Pinus sylvestris</i>), but also has the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norway_spruce\" target=\"_blank\">Norway spruce</a> (<i>Picea abies</i>). The pines can attain a great height, particularly those around Lake Rittak, in the south of the park. The undergrowth is mostly covered with <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moss\" target=\"_blank\">mosses</a> and <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lichen\" target=\"_blank\">lichens</a>, in particular <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cladonia_rangiferina\" target=\"_blank\">reindeer lichen</a>, and also with <i><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vaccinium_myrtillus\" target=\"_blank\">Vaccinium myrtillus</a></i>, <i><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Empetrum_nigrum\" target=\"_blank\">Empetrum nigrum</a></i> and <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vaccinium_vitis-idaea\" target=\"_blank\">cowberry</a> (<i>Vaccinium vitis-idaea</i>).</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">These forests are a privileged habitat for numerous species of animals. Among the large carnivores, the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown_bear\" target=\"_blank\">brown bear</a> (<i>Ursus arctos</i>) is particularly frequent in the park and in the neighbouring Stora Sj\u00f6fallet. The bear also ventures into the subalpine region too fairly often. The <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eurasian_Lynx\" target=\"_blank\">Eurasian Lynx</a> (<i>Lynx lynx</i>), classed as an <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Endangered_species\" target=\"_blank\">endangered species</a> in Sweden, is also found around the lakes of Rittak and Laitaure, but also goes to the subalpine forests of Rapa Valley. The <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_fox\" target=\"_blank\">red fox</a> (<i>Vulpes vulpes</i>) is relatively frequent, and little by little is extending its territory towards the higher zones, so it competes with the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arctic_fox\" target=\"_blank\">Arctic fox</a>, (<i>Vulpes lagopus</i>). In terms of small mammals, the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pine_marten\" target=\"_blank\">pine marten</a> (<i>Martes martes</i>), the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Least_weasel\" target=\"_blank\">least weasel</a> (<i>Mustela nivalis</i>) and the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stoat\" target=\"_blank\">stoat</a> (<i>Mustela erminea</i>) are very frequent, but the ermine also lives easily on the higher regions too. The herbivores include a very large number of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moose\" target=\"_blank\">moose</a> (<i>Alces alces</i>) as the forests and humid zones provide them with a lot of food.<sup><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sarek_National_Park#cite_note-Curry-Lindahl64-40\" target=\"_blank\">[40]</a></sup> They often grow to an impressive size in the park, with enormous <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antler\" target=\"_blank\">antlers</a>.<sup><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sarek_National_Park#cite_note-Curry-Lindahl65-41\" target=\"_blank\">[41]</a></sup></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/158702-advises-on-running-shadow-realm?p=158731#post158731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any notable scenarios with the local spirit courts that impact the area?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not thought on any - could you give some good examples on those?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-04-2014, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T08:22:59-07:00","id":159076,"title":"","content":"Here's my best advice on running things in the Shadow.<br /> <br /> 1) Don't worry about the <i>actual </i>terrain as much as the <i>impressionist </i>terrain. Does the area <b>look </b>rocky and dangerous in the material realm? Then it probably is. Does it <b>look </b>like it might be filled with tranquil lakes and easy trails in the material realm? Then it probably is. The Shadow is a reflection of the <i>impressions </i>and <i>feelings </i>of the area. If no one is sure what's up there, then it might look more foreboding with dark areas due to the extreme tree cover, which also makes it a little claustrophobic.<br /> <br /> 2) I usually treat the interactions with the spirits in the Shadow like an amusement park horror house, but instead of people in masks wandering around, they let loose a bunch of wild animals. The characters will wander thru stretches of general shadowy areas, then suddenly something will jump out at them, and it'll either disappear just as suddenly or go straight for the characters. The weaker (prey) spirits will jump thru and scamper back off into the darkness. The stronger (predator) spirits will see potential prey in the characters and go after them. A quick, ferocious, and bloody battle takes place and then the whole place gets quiet again. Too quiet. Like everybody's watching now.<br /> <br /> 3) Not every spirit is <b>awake</b>. The majority of the spirits are just filling in the exact space that their material counterpart has. The tree spirits are there for the trees. The rock spirits are there as rocks. The wild sheep and rams spirits are just grazing on the grass spirits and the grass isn't trying to move away from them. Most of them are barely beyond motes. The dangerous ones are the ones who have started to stray from their material anchors. These are the ones who've been snacking on other spirits that may or may not be an acceptable part of it's diet. The owl spirit who's been dining on mice and rabbits is fine. The owl spirit feeding on darkness and flight spirits is just getting more specialized, but still not far off from where it started. The owl spirit who's been scooping up <i>wolf </i>spirits and <i>tree</i> spirits.......<i><b>that thing ain't right!!</b></i><br /> <br /> 4) While spirits are generally hostile to the Uratha, not all of them will outright <i>attack </i>them. Some of them are small enough and weak enough to know they don't stand a chance. So they run and they hide and they <b><i><u>WATCH</u></i></b><u><i><b>!</b></i></u> Oh my goodness, the number of eyes staring out from the darkness in the Shadow is enough to make even the most level-headed turn paranoid. And what are they watching for? An opportunity. Maybe the characters know a way out to the material realm. Maybe something bigger will come along and rough them up enough to make them easy picking. Maybe something will just tear them apart and the others can take the scraps. While not every spirit will <i>attack</i>, they are still willing to become a <i>predator</i> (or scavenger) if the prey is weak enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T09:06:45-07:00","id":159120,"title":"","content":"The Shadow is a place of horror. It's the haunted house you have to enter, the recurring nightmare you're worried about dreaming every night, and occasionally it's the battlefield you're conscripted to fight on, against your will. The Shadow part of your territory might be different, but only insofar as it's a place of horror you're intimately familiar with.<br /> <br /> Remember that the Hisil is a place of meaning, spirituality and, quite literally, a Shadow of the Flesh. Spirit encounters should never be random. You don't get to face some anger spirit, you'll face the embodied wrath of a teenager about to go on a killing spree in his school. The murder spirit trying to rip your guts out is an idealized reflection of that serial killer who slaughtered a two digit number of people in the city decades ago. The lust spirit trying to seduce you - it's the PC's own repressed feelings of sexuality, trying desperately to find a release.<br /> <br /> Remember also that, most times, you can't meaningfully, permanently change the Shadow without also changing the Flesh. Spirits you tear apart will quite simply reform and come back to haunt you once they have gathered sufficient essence. Spirits are fought by changing the Flesh so that they lack appropriate sources of essence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Don't rely on logic. Spirits aren't exactly a model of constancy. The interesting thing about the Shadow is that as soon as you draw a box around it and say &quot;this is the Shadow, and this is what its inhabitants are like&quot;, it pokes a tentacle through the box and reminds you that you missed a spot. And if you follow that tentacle, you'll only discover that it goes on forever.<br /> <br /> That's how the spirit realm works. It defies common sense. It doesn't have to operate according to rules that can be understood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T09:11:16-07:00","id":159122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/158702-advises-on-running-shadow-realm#post158702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I don't have ideas on 2-3 scenes of interaction and travel in between, so players would get they first taste of Shadow Realm, like in books. Any advises how to improve this?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?t=254403\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?t=254403</a><br /> <br /> Hope this helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T09:49:38-07:00","id":159153,"title":"","content":"<b>Papa Bear</b>, thanks for great description of &quot;Shadow Realm Rules&quot; - I finally get this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Christian</b>, thanks for link, I will be ssssooo much useful as to trying to kill PCs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/158702-advises-on-running-shadow-realm?p=159120#post159120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that the Hisil is a place of meaning, spirituality and, quite literally, a Shadow of the Flesh. Spirit encounters should never be random. You don't get to face some anger spirit, you'll face the embodied wrath of a teenager about to go on a killing spree in his school. The murder spirit trying to rip your guts out is an idealized reflection of that serial killer who slaughtered a two digit number of people in the city decades ago. The lust spirit trying to seduce you - it's the PC's own repressed feelings of sexuality, trying desperately to find a release.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hee is a thing - I get how &quot;ecology&quot; works. But I have problem with transplating it to, for example, mountain range. We got Point A ( Waterfalll Verge ) and Point B ( Bear's Graveyard, Totem-to-be &quot;domain&quot; ), but I don't know how to run the game between them. <b>Papa Bear</b>'s and your advices helps it a lot in this, but still I'm open on good ideas for encounters and ideas to run with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T10:07:08-07:00","id":159172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/158702-advises-on-running-shadow-realm?p=159153#post159153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hee is a thing - I get how &quot;ecology&quot; works. But I have problem with transplating it to, for example, mountain range. We got Point A ( Waterfalll Verge ) and Point B ( Bear's Graveyard, Totem-to-be &quot;domain&quot; ), but I don't know how to run the game between them. <b>Papa Bear</b>'s and your advices helps it a lot in this, but still I'm open on good ideas for encounters and ideas to run with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Try this - start with figuring out where the Bear's Graveyard is in relation to the Waterfall.<br /> <br /> Is it up the mountain? Then they'll encounter more spirits related to higher elevations and what exists up there. More snow and cold and rocks, less animals and trees, the avalanche spirits <i>love </i>to eat wandering people in waves of snow and ice.<br /> <br /> Is is across the glade in the hidden valley? Then they'll encounter more plant and animal spirits, negotiating with the mountain goats to cross the glen without a fight. The goats are <i>very </i>territorial and with ram the shit out of anyone who tries to just stroll across their glade.<br /> <br /> Is it under the lake? Then they have to figure out how to convince the salmon spirits to take them down there. The salmon offer to have them ride in their mouths......yeah, that's not <i>too </i>obvious, is it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar"